WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.245 --> 00:00:03.585
- It’s not very many people really know,

00:00:03.585 --> 00:00:07.662
but the Great Lakes has
thousands of shipwrecks.

00:00:07.662 --> 00:00:11.454
In Wisconsin for sure, we know we have 750

00:00:11.454 --> 00:00:13.538
historic shipwreck losses.

00:00:13.538 --> 00:00:16.367
(upbeat music)

00:00:16.367 --> 00:00:18.707
My name is Caitlin Zant, and
I'm a maritime archaeologist

00:00:18.707 --> 00:00:21.874
with the Wisconsin Historical Society.

00:00:23.184 --> 00:00:25.512
I would say the main goal of what we do

00:00:25.512 --> 00:00:28.170
in maritime archaeology is to preserve

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:30.272
our maritime history
and also the history of

00:00:30.272 --> 00:00:32.561
the United States in general.

00:00:32.561 --> 00:00:34.748
The ships are quite sturdy,

00:00:34.748 --> 00:00:36.977
but they've also been underwater for

00:00:36.977 --> 00:00:39.227
up to a hundred, 150 years.

00:00:40.811 --> 00:00:42.607
Our shipwrecks don't disappear over time

00:00:42.607 --> 00:00:44.802
like they do in the oceans.

00:00:44.802 --> 00:00:46.719
The fresh water that's very cold

00:00:46.719 --> 00:00:48.008
actually does a really good job at

00:00:48.008 --> 00:00:50.428
preserving these shipwrecks.

00:00:50.428 --> 00:00:52.388
One of the really great
things about Lake Michigan

00:00:52.388 --> 00:00:54.043
that makes it really unique

00:00:54.043 --> 00:00:57.728
is the fact that you do
have fresh, clear water.

00:00:57.728 --> 00:01:00.692
You can see many times,
especially on deep wrecks

00:01:00.692 --> 00:01:03.059
a hundred to 150 feet.

00:01:03.059 --> 00:01:04.892
When you are down there
looking at a shipwreck

00:01:04.892 --> 00:01:07.819
you start to think of all the
sailors that sailed on it,

00:01:07.819 --> 00:01:08.952
or if it was a passenger ship,

00:01:08.952 --> 00:01:11.303
the passengers that happened to be on it.

00:01:11.303 --> 00:01:14.693
You can still find pieces of clothing

00:01:14.693 --> 00:01:17.493
in certain areas, buttons, shoes,

00:01:17.493 --> 00:01:19.423
and so that really gives insight

00:01:19.423 --> 00:01:22.242
to the lives of these sailors.

00:01:22.242 --> 00:01:25.528
There's definitely a little
bit of a thrill of discovery.

00:01:25.528 --> 00:01:27.917
When we go down on a ship,

00:01:27.917 --> 00:01:29.559
even on a ship that we know,

00:01:29.559 --> 00:01:30.903
we think we know what it is.

00:01:30.903 --> 00:01:33.170
There's still always that little

00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:35.051
sense of excitement that
you're gonna find something

00:01:35.051 --> 00:01:37.706
that no one else has seen before.

00:01:37.706 --> 00:01:39.186
(water gurgling)

00:01:39.186 --> 00:01:42.980
(playful ambient music)

00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:45.049
(water gurgles)

